  "id": "Compound::DB00701 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Amprenavir is linked to Cyp2c8 through a series of metabolic and enzymatic interactions. The evidence suggests that Amprenavir binds to Cyp2b6, which is involved in the metabolism of diclofenac and arachidonic acid, both of which are processed by Cyp2c8. This implies that Amprenavir may indirectly influence Cyp2c8 through its interaction with Cyp2b6, which is part of a broader metabolic pathway involving Cyp2c8. Additionally, Amprenavir is classified as a inhibitor of Cytochrome P450 3a4, and Amiodarone, a member of this class, binds to Cyp2c8. This suggests that the inhibition of Cyp2b6 by Amprenavir could lead to a downstream effect on Cyp2c8, potentially altering its activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Amprenavir influences Cyp2c8, though the exact nature of this relationship remains partially inferred.",
